          "<code>edit_file</code> takes <code>ops</code>, each one of <code>replace</code>, <code>delete</code>, <code>insert_before</code> or <code>insert_after</code> with a 1-based <code>start</code>; <code>replace</code> and <code>delete</code> also state <code>end</code>, the last line they cover, and one without it is refused as <code>edit op \"replace\" needs end (or endLine): the last line it covers</code> rather than read as one line. An undeclared op is refused naming every op. The anchored <code>edit</code> tool resolves its <code>SWAP</code>, <code>DEL</code> and <code>INS</code> hunks to these same edits, and <code>write_archive</code> (<code>upsert</code>, <code>delete</code>) and <code>write_sqlite</code> (<code>insert</code>, <code>update</code>, <code>delete</code>) refuse an action outside their own list by naming it.",
